{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"0b0bf20ee3ba03a6c08a6278196290214664b2a53ebe30578f6d55a30d871b95","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011tHPq7EmpgBoXJZQt6DZD2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app && cat > /tmp/codex_prompt.txt <<'EOF'\nDo not change anything: read-only diagnosis. Answer in Russian, briefly, for the owner, plus the technical reason.\n\nNexo is a FlClash (mihomo/Clash.Meta core, in core/Clash.Meta) based Android/macOS VPN client in this repository.\nFacts measured by the owner today: on the very same network (Mac tethered through a phone), the Vienna node FAILS in Nexo while the Brazil node works; in Karing (sing-box based) BOTH Vienna and Brazil work. Other customers carry traffic through Vienna, the server is healthy.\nEarlier measurements with plain mihomo 1.19.33 on the owner's home path to Vienna: about 3 requests pass, then every request fails with \"context deadline exceeded\" for minutes; fingerprint variants safari/chrome made no clear difference in that earlier test, which may have been disturbed.\n\nVienna node as the subscription gives it to Karing: vless, tcp, security=tls, sni=<domain>, fp=chrome, alpn=h2, flow=xtls-rprx-vision, port 443. Server: haproxy on 443 in TCP mode routes by SNI/ALPN; SNI+h2 goes to Xray 127.0.0.1:2097, tcp+tls+vision.\nBrazil node: vless, tcp, security=reality, sni=www.google.com, fp=chrome, flow=xtls-rprx-vision.\n\nVienna node as the server generates it for Nexo (mihomo YAML): type vless, server IP, port 443, network tcp, udp true, tls true, servername <domain>, client-fingerprint safari, flow xtls-rprx-vision, alpn [h2]. DNS in the profile: fake-ip, respect-rules true, nameserver DoH 1.1.1.1 and 1.0.0.1, proxy-server-nameserver 77.88.8.8. The auto group is url-test, interval 20, timeout 3000, tolerance 250, url gstatic generate_204. unified-delay true.\n\nQuestion: what in mihomo's VLESS + Vision + TLS (uTLS fingerprint, ALPN h2, XTLS Vision padding, connection reuse, UDP over xudp, etc.) can differ from sing-box's behaviour so that this node fails in mihomo but works in sing-box, while a Reality node works in both? Read the mihomo source under core/Clash.Meta (transport/vless, component/tls, adapter/outbound/vless.go). Give ranked hypotheses, each with the file and line that supports it and one concrete test to prove or refute it.\nEOF\ncodex exec --sandbox read-only --skip-git-repo-check -C /Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app -m gpt-6.1-sol - < /tmp/codex_prompt.txt > /tmp/codex_out.txt 2>&1; tail -70 /tmp/codex_out.txt; rm -f /tmp/codex_prompt.txt","description":"Ask Codex for an independent read-only diagnosis","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ZHLEQ3LhdYnwTfxhbidUS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=\"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad\"; netstat -rn -f inet | awk '$1==\"default\"{print $2,$NF}' | head -5; route -n get 1.1.1.1 | grep interface; umask 077; cat > \"$SP/variants.py\" <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Same network, same server, several mihomo settings for the Vienna node, bound to the physical interface so Karing's tunnel is not involved.\"\"\"\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlsplit\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nIFACE = sys.argv[1]\nline = [l for l in open(os.path.join(HERE, \"mihomo-test\", \"links.txt\")) if \"152.53.50.204\" in l][0].strip()\nu = urlsplit(line); q = {k: v[0] for k, v in parse_qs(u.query).items()}\nbase = {\"type\": \"vless\", \"server\": u.hostname, \"port\": u.port, \"uuid\": u.username, \"network\": \"tcp\", \"tls\": True, \"servername\": q[\"sni\"], \"flow\": q[\"flow\"]}\nV = {\n \"A safari h2 udp (Nexo now)\": dict(base, **{\"client-fingerprint\": \"safari\", \"alpn\": [\"h2\"], \"udp\": True}),\n \"B chrome h2 udp (as Karing link)\": dict(base, **{\"client-fingerprint\": \"chrome\", \"alpn\": [\"h2\"], \"udp\": True}),\n \"C firefox h2\": dict(base, **{\"client-fingerprint\": \"firefox\", \"alpn\": [\"h2\"], \"udp\": True}),\n \"D no fingerprint h2\": dict(base, **{\"alpn\": [\"h2\"], \"udp\": True}),\n}\nports = {}\nproxies, listeners = [], []\nfor i, (name, p) in enumerate(V.items()):\n    n = \"p%d\" % i; proxies.append(dict(p, name=n)); ports[name] = 19100 + i\n    listeners.append({\"name\": \"l%d\" % i, \"type\": \"mixed\", \"port\": ports[name], \"proxy\": n})\nwd = os.path.join(HERE, \"var\"); os.makedirs(wd, exist_ok=True)\njson.dump({\"mixed-port\": 19099, \"mode\": \"rule\", \"ipv6\": False, \"log-level\": \"warning\", \"interface-name\": IFACE, \"proxies\": proxies, \"listeners\": listeners, \"rules\": [\"MATCH,DIRECT\"]}, open(wd + \"/config.yaml\", \"w\"))\ncore = subprocess.Popen([os.path.join(HERE, \"mihomo-test/bin/mihomo-darwin-arm64-v1.19.33\"), \"-d\", wd, \"-f\", wd + \"/config.yaml\"], stdout=open(wd + \"/run.log\", \"w\"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\ntime.sleep(3)\nres = {k: [] for k in V}\ntry:\n    for r in range(10):\n        for name, port in ports.items():\n            out = subprocess.run([\"curl\", \"-s\", \"-o\", \"/dev/null\", \"-m\", \"6\", \"--noproxy\", \"\", \"-x\", \"http://127.0.0.1:%d\" % port, \"-w\", \"%{http_code}\", \"https://www.gstatic.com/generate_204\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n            res[name].append(\".\" if out == \"204\" else \"x\")\n        time.sleep(1)\n    for name, port in ports.items():\n        out = subprocess.run([\"curl\", \"-s\", \"-m\", \"8\", \"--noproxy\", \"\", \"-x\", \"http://127.0.0.1:%d\" % port, \"https://api.ipify.org\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n        print(\"%-34s %s  exit %s\" % (name, \"\".join(res[name]), out[:16]), flush=True)\nfinally:\n    core.terminate(); core.wait()\nlog = re.sub(r\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f-]{27}\", \"<id>\", open(wd + \"/run.log\").read())\nerrs = {}\nfor m in re.finditer(r'dial (p\\d).*?error: ([^\"]{0,80})', log):\n    errs[(m.group(1), m.group(2)[:70])] = errs.get((m.group(1), m.group(2)[:70]), 0) + 1\nfor k, v in sorted(errs.items()): print(k, v)\nPY\nIF=$(netstat -rn -f inet | awk '$1==\"default\" && $NF !~ /utun/{print $NF; exit}'); echo \"physical: $IF\"; ifconfig \"$IF\" | grep 'inet ' | cut -c1-40; python3 \"$SP/variants.py\" \"$IF\"; rm -rf \"$SP/var\"","description":"Test Vienna node settings directly on the current network","timeout":280000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
