{"parentUuid":"6f60f516-527c-47f1-960e-108fb01d70af","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Fz6XPAVq88DAMywNdwvuvT","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: No stderr output","stdout":"","exitCode":1,"command":"command hook 2","durationMs":8},"type":"attachment","uuid":"31db7aa6-220d-4178-9880-8e863b17fed0","timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:31:51.265Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"fix/adaptive-headers","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"6f60f516-527c-47f1-960e-108fb01d70af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"39216578-7bc9-46d7-8b42-154505c1dbdc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fz6XPAVq88DAMywNdwvuvT","type":"tool_result","content":"29:- `rust_api`'s `ipc` module provides the native local-IPC primitives: a Unix domain socket on macOS/Linux and a named pipe\n32:- `lib/core/service.dart` (`CoreService`) is the composition root. It wires the IPC transport, launcher selection,\n42:- `lib/core/desktop/launcher.dart` abstracts direct child-process and privileged Helper ownership through idempotent process\n43:  leases. `lib/core/desktop/helper_client.dart` is the typed local HTTP client for the privileged Helper.\n165:The Windows Helper answers only a connection whose client process runs under the owner SID it was installed for;\n166:the Linux Helper only the owner uid. A setuid Core is executable by `root:admin` (macOS) or the installing user's primary\n169:or a remote party reaching the privileged Core's control or filesystem APIs is a vulnerability.\n171:A process running as the same account is not stopped. It can ask the Helper to start the Core\n173:a privileged Core: `initClash` chooses the home directory every path check anchors on, and `getConfig`,\n176:distinguish it from a same-account process that can already read FlClash's memory and files. This remains a user-to-root\n177:or user-to-SYSTEM privilege escalation, not a complete security fix. An open external\n182:Closing the same-account case requires limiting what a hijacked Core can do. Keeping the main Core unprivileged and\n183:moving host changes into narrow platform helpers requires architectural work, but need not introduce repeated prompts\n184:or remove ordinary proxy functionality. Features that require additional privileges, such as identifying other users'\n186:paths; intentional external symlink targets need explicit allowed roots. These changes have not been implemented.\n188:privileged filesystem operations available to the host. Changes must not widen access to those operations.\n263:  the process PID returned by the Helper lease.\n273:Direct launch is used on macOS, inside an AppImage, and as the Windows/Linux fallback when the privileged Helper is not\n274:ready. When the Helper is ready, it owns the Core child and Dart owns it through a session-scoped lease.\n512:`test/helpers/test_app.dart` in its builder, as `TestApp` does.\n541:reference for the metaphor. Tests find one with `find.byGlyph` from `test/helpers/glyph_finders.dart`.\n547:`GlyphIcon` written inside such a button; an icon that reaches the button from elsewhere, as through a helper that picks\n661:- A pane over one painted before it in the same root reads a second image, a level up, with the first drawn in as\n667:  root is the host or its nearest ancestor that draws offscreen: as a backdrop filter would there, it\n669:  `LiquidGlassFade` is no root: as Core Animation fades a layer, its panes still read what lies behind it and fade with\n712:- Without Impeller's shader filters (Skia on the Intel macOS build, `flutter test`) a pane frosts from its capture:\n917:there is none, and everything goes on the root navigator, `rootNavigatorKey` in `lib/ui/navigator.dart`. A route\n923:The root navigator is only for what belongs to no single destination:\n925:- dialogs, which `dialogs` in `lib/common/dialog.dart` hosts on the root unless it is given a context, and the notifier;\n929:Never reach for the root to open a page or sheet from a page, whether through `rootNavigatorKey`,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fd69c47e-4bc3-4fe3-8b7c-8f6cc106b04f","timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:31:52.372Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"29:- `rust_api`'s `ipc` module provides the native local-IPC primitives: a Unix domain socket on macOS/Linux and a named pipe\n32:- `lib/core/service.dart` (`CoreService`) is the composition root. It wires the IPC transport, launcher selection,\n42:- `lib/core/desktop/launche