ts/100-russia-introduces-whitelists"},{"title":"github.com%2Fhyperion cs%2Fdpi checkers","url":"https://awesome.ecosyste.ms/projects/github.com%2Fhyperion-cs%2Fdpi-checkers"},{"title":"github was blocked 2016","url":"https://tproger.ru/news/github-was-blocked-2016"}]},"The search didn't turn up the `vadim-tolmachev/allowlist-probe` repository, so I can't confirm what it contains. The results did cover related projects on Russian internet allowlists.\n\n- **Russia mobile whitelist repos:** A repo by kort0881 tracks mobile-network whitelists in Russia and describes VPN and Telegram as blocked there. It lists a current whitelist file and working configs. Another, hxehex's russia-mobile-internet-whitelist, covers strategies for bypassing mobile internet whitelists.\n- **Allowlist mechanics:** One explainer describes an allowlist as the opposite of ordinary blocking: only listed resources are allowed and everything else is closed by default. It also notes that VPNs most often do not work either under an allowlist, because filtering happens at the network level.\n- **Probing tools:** The hyperion-cs/dpi-checkers project lets you test an internet provider for censorship. It includes a domain whitelist checker, which may be closest in purpose to an allowlist probe.\n- **Official stance on GitHub:** Russia's telecoms watchdog said in May 2026 that GitHub is not being blocked in Russia.\n\nIf you have the repo's exact URL or a description, I can search again to check it."],"durationSeconds":5.132585583999753,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2180d2a6-1ba3-4dee-99f8-a9ad3a6dbd27","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","root":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","branch":"feat/desktop-tun","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Shahen777/nexo-app","visibili