{"parentUuid":"025651f3-e148-4722-9a71-e1c950f0425e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrK4fqKQHVUGt5UWy3RB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F6tUrneijXzAFntDhmrzEd","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/frank-underwood64/whitelists_bypass/discussions/1","prompt":"Explain exactly the CDN + XHTTP whitelist bypass: which CDN (Russian CDN providers in whitelist like CDNvideo, Yandex CDN, VK, EdgeCenter, Selectel CDN?), how domain/SNI/Host are set, xhttp mode, origin setup, what was tested on which operator, limitations and date. Also comments' results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3429,"cache_read_input_tokens":134756,"output_tokens":223,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3429,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":134756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3429},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01F6tUrneijXzAFntDhmrzEd":{"url":"https://github.com/frank-underwood64/whitelists_bypass/discussions/1","prompt":"Explain exactly the CDN + XHTTP whitelist bypass: which CDN (Russian CDN providers in whitelist like CDNvideo, Yandex CDN, VK, EdgeCenter, Selectel CDN?), how domain/SNI/Host are set, xhttp mode, origin setup, what was tested on which operator, limitations and date. Also comments' results."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e1afe73-b055-45ab-87b7-bbe183e887cf","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgrK4fef49nuWSUJJWWKB","requestRef":"7e356c05-ca86-491d-a7b1-242e2da711de","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0110d92-bbb6-4e6c-a54f-7ba3eebb6714","timestamp":"2026-11-08T23:15:57.793Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"feat/desktop-tun","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"f0110d92-bbb6-4e6c-a54f-7ba3eebb6714","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"91d163fa-4c33-4181-a871-4269cd8b22ce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6tUrneijXzAFntDhmrzEd","type":"tool_result","content":"The page is a promotional discussion thread. It describes the architecture in general terms but withholds the working parameters, which the author sells privately through Telegram. I can't give an exact configuration from it, but here is what it says.\n\n**Architecture (as described)**\n- Client → HTTPS to a CDN distribution domain → CDN → HTTPS to a source domain → nginx on a VPS → local Xray inbound (VLESS over XHTTP).\n- Two domains are used, each with its own TLS certificate. nginx forwards only a specific path to Xray and serves a normal site or stub elsewhere.\n- The origin certificate must match the name the CDN uses to connect. Host-header and origin-host settings differ by provider.\n- The stated XHTTP mode is packet-up: upstream uses several POST requests, and downstream uses a streaming GET. The page says the client needs a recent Xray build and names Happ and INCY as working clients.\n\n**CDNs named**\n- Named as candidates: Yandex, VK, Beeline, Selectel, Timeweb, Beget.\n- Beeline and its underlying provider were described as offering a free tier, which the author says is now being blocked.\n- Later comments report Yandex, VK, Selectel, Beeline, and Timeweb as working, though some of these reports are contested.\n- CDNvideo doesn't appear in the page. EdgeCenter was asked about, and the author said it isn't the service he uses.\n\n**Operators and regions (reported, unverified)**\n- The author says it works on mobile networks in general but gives no per-operator data.\n- One commenter in the Volga region says Megafon and Beeline issues were resolved, and that Yandex works.\n- One Crimea commenter says Yandex, MWS, and Beeline work over wired connections but not on mobile base stations.\n- One commenter says Timeweb's main site now won't load under restrictions.\n- One commenter spent about 10 hours failing with Selectel, then switched to Yandex Cloud and got it working, noting the CDN throttles VPN traffic.\n\n**Limitations reported**\n- Method restrictions: one commenter says Yandex blocks POST. The author disputes this and says GET works.\n- Body and header problems: some payloads are cut off without chunking, and packet-up works but poorly for some users.\n- Account blocks: several commenters report cloud accounts being blocked, including on free tiers.\n- The post says Yandex expects the origin to respond within five seconds, and raising the nginx timeout doesn't change that.\n- One user reports Telegram media failing on Yandex.\n\n**Comment results**\n- Positive: several users thank the author and say the setup works on VK, Timeweb, or Beeline.\n- Negative: one buyer says a $50 guide didn't work, another says registration failed, and another accuses the author of deleting comments.\n- The author promotes paid guides ($30–50), setup services, reseller arrangements, and a \"new\" CDN with no name given. Many commenters are also promoting services.\n\nThe thread runs from July 27 to October 16, 2026, and the captured text is truncated. Nothing here is independently verified, and the mixed reports and paid-service promotion mean the claims should be treated with caution."}]},"uuid":"851bcbd6-9f58-451e-9e22-a1517d6bcfbe","timestamp":"2026-11-08T23:16:18.285Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":1212403,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page is a promotional discussion thread. It describes the architecture in general terms but withholds the working parameters, which the author sells privately through Telegram. I can't give an exact configuration from it, but here is what it says.\n\n**Architecture (as described)**\n- Client → HTTPS to a CDN distribution domain → CDN → HTTPS to a source domain → nginx on a VPS → local Xray inbound (VLESS over XHTTP).\n- Two domains are used, each with its own TLS certificate. nginx forwards only a specific path to Xray and serves a normal site or stub elsewhere.\n- The origin certificate must match the name the CDN uses to connect. Host-header and origin-host settings differ by provider.\n- The stated XHTTP mode is packet-up: upstream uses several POST requests, and downstream uses a streaming GET. The page says the client needs a recent Xray build and names Happ and INCY as working clients.\n\n**CDNs named**\n- Named as candidates: Yandex, VK, Beeline, Selectel, Timeweb, Beget.\n- Beeline and its underlying provider were described as offering a free tier, which the author says is now being blocked.\n- Later comments report Yandex, VK, Selectel, Beeline, and Timeweb as working, though some of these reports are contested.\n- CDNvideo doesn't appear in the page. EdgeCenter was asked about, and the author said it isn't the service he uses.\n\n**Operators and regions (reported, unverified)**\n- The author says it works on mobile networks in general but gives no per-operator data.\n- One commenter in the Volga region says Megafon and Beeline issues were resolved, and that Yandex works.\n- One Crimea commenter says Yandex, MWS, and Beeline work over wired connections but not on mobile base stations.\n- One commenter says Timeweb's main site now won't load under restrictions.\n- One commenter spent about 10 hours failing with Selectel, then switched to Yandex Cloud and got it working, noting the CDN throttles VPN traffic.\n\n**Limitations reported**\n- Method restrictions: one commenter says Yandex blocks POST. The author disputes this and says GET works.\n- Body and header problems: some payloads are cut off without chunking, and packet-up works but poorly for some users.\n- Account blocks: several commenters report cloud accounts being blocked, including on free tiers.\n- The post says Yandex expects the origin to respond within five seconds, and raising the nginx timeout doesn't change that.\n- One user reports Telegram media failing on Yandex.\n\n**Comment results**\n- Positive: several users thank the author and say the setup works on VK, Timeweb, or Beeline.\n- Negative: one buyer says a $50 guide didn't work, another says registration failed, and another accuses the author of deleting comments.\n- The author promotes paid guides ($30–50), setup services, reseller arrangements, and a \"new\" CDN with no name given. Many commenters are also promoting services.\n\nThe thread runs from July 27 to October 16, 2026, and the captured text is truncated. Nothing here is independently verified, and the mixed reports and paid-service promotion mean the claims should be treated with caution.","durationMs":20070,"url":"https://github.com/frank-underwood64/whitelists_bypass/discussions/1"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3e1afe73-b055-45ab-87b7-bbe183e887cf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","root":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","branch":"feat/desktop-tun","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Shahen777/nexo-app","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Shahen777/nexo-app","visibility":"public"},{"name":"upstream","host":"github.com","remote":"chen08209/FlClash","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Shahen777/nexo-app","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0110d92-bbb6-4e6c-a54f-7ba3eebb6714","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"feat/desktop-tu